      "description": "Recommendation 1: Edit 59510 and 59514 to bundle into global obstetric services when billed by the provider or provider group under the 'same TIN' for the same pregnancy episode, and deny duplicate payment beyond 'one cesarean delivery' / 'one cesarean only'; allow separate payment only for a 'problem oriented diagnosis' or 'unrelated condition'. Apply to all states. Exempt: problem oriented diagnosis, unrelated condition. Peer: Centene and United Health both flag 59510/59514 in maternity component logic, and Centene limits payment to 'one cesarean delivery' / 'one cesarean only'..\n\nRecommendation 2: Edit 59409, 59410, and 59430 to pay separately only 'after delivery' and, for postpartum component review, apply the 'within 72 hours of delivery' and 'same TIN' checks; otherwise bundle these component codes back to the full maternity package. Apply to all states. Peer: Cigna and United Health both restrict these component claims to 'after delivery'; Cigna also adds a 'within 72 hours of delivery' check..\n\nIA \u2014 Implement utilization review on antepartum codes 59425 and 59426 using the peer thresholds '4-6 visits for 59425' and '7+ visits for 59426'; treat '13 routine prenatal visits' as routine global care and only consider separate payment for visits 'beyond 13 routine visits', except 'complication E&M' or 'unrelated condition E&M'. (all states) Cigna and United Health both use '4-6 visits for 59425' and '7+ visits for 59426' thresholds for antepartum-only billing.. Exempt: complication E&M, unrelated condition E&M.",
